/* book Worked example: Q: A thermometer reads 27 °C. Convert this temperature to K, °F and R.
   1. Given: t(°C) = 27 °C.
   2. Kelvin: T(K) = 27 + 273.15 = 300.15 K.
   3. Fahrenheit: t(°F) = 1.8 × 27 + 32 = 48.6 + 32 = 80.6 °F.
   4. Rankine: T(R) = 80.6 + 459.67 = 540.27 R. Check: 1.8 × 300.15 = 540.27 R.
   Answer: 27 °C equals 300.15 K, 80.6 °F and 540.27 R. */
